    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀβληχρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>
		euphon., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βληχρός,</span>
			q.v.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>weak,
				feeble,</i> of Aphrodite's hand, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.337
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τείχεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.178
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span> an <i>easy</i>
			death in ripe old age, opp. a <i>violent</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.135
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.282
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Sent.Vat.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.205
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρετός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procop.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					2.22
				</span></i>
			.</div>
